  "brief": {
    "story": "The parts drawer only has 74HC00 NAND chips, and the safety interlock needs AND: the press runs only with both guards closed. A NAND followed by an inverter is AND, and a NAND with its inputs tied together is an inverter.",
    "goal": "Wire gate 1’s output (pin 3) into gate 2 (pins 4 and 5, already tied together) so LED1 = SA AND SB.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "74HC00 · quad NAND",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Gate 1",
          "pins 1, 2 → 3"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 2",
          "pins 4, 5 → 6 (4 and 5 tied)"
        ],
        [
          "SA, SB",
          "pins 1, 2"
        ],
        [
          "LED1",
          "from pin 6"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Gate 1 already gives NAND(SA, SB) on pin 3 (column 12). Gate 2 has its inputs tied, so it inverts.",
    "Feed pin 3 into gate 2: NOT(NAND) = AND.",
    "One wire from column 12 (pin 3) to column 13 (pin 4)."
  ],
